A procedure missing its :ENDPROC is followed directly by the next
:PROCEDURE, whose :ENDPROC is present. Records how the block scanner
pairs the single :ENDPROC between two open procedures: the expected shape
is one unclosed_block finding, not a cascade (diag.unclosed_block,
diag.mismatched_block_end).
-- input.ssl --
:PROCEDURE LoadHeader;
	:PARAMETERS sKey;
	:RETURN "H-" + sKey;

:PROCEDURE LoadDetail;
	:PARAMETERS sKey;
	:RETURN "D-" + sKey;
:ENDPROC;
-- format --
:PROCEDURE LoadHeader;
	:PARAMETERS sKey;

	:RETURN "H-" + sKey;

	:PROCEDURE LoadDetail;
		:PARAMETERS sKey;

		:RETURN "D-" + sKey;
	:ENDPROC;
-- diagnostics --
1:1-1:11 error unclosed_block: Unclosed ':PROCEDURE' - expected ':ENDPROC'
-- diagnostics [--strict --info] --
1:1-1:11 error unclosed_block: Unclosed ':PROCEDURE' - expected ':ENDPROC'
